<figure class="prepared" data-r34-prepared aria-labelledby="r34-prepared-title"><figcaption id="r34-prepared-title"><span>Figure 1</span> What does the planner know about status?</figcaption>
<label>Query and plan <select><option value="custom">Custom · status supplied as pending</option><option value="generic">Generic · status remains $2</option><option value="literal">Generic · pending is fixed in SQL</option></select></label>
<div class="flow" data-live><div><b>Query condition</b><p data-predicate>shop_id = 20 AND status = 'pending'</p></div><div><b>Partial-index proof</b><p data-proof>The answer lies within status = 'pending'.</p></div><div><b>Observed route</b><p data-route>Ordered index-only scan → Limit 10</p></div></div>
<p class="result" data-result aria-live="polite">3 local buffer accesses at Limit; 10 rows returned.</p>
<details><summary>Read all three observed routes</summary><p>Custom with pending uses the partial index and three local buffer accesses. Generic with an unknown status scans 2,048 heap pages and sorts. Generic with pending fixed in SQL uses the partial index and three local accesses. Each returns the same first ten pending order IDs for shop 20. These counts come from the native fixture; the boxes explain the proof, rather than simulating PostgreSQL.</p></details>
<p class="caption">One PostgreSQL 18.6 run with a deliberately sparse index: <code>(shop_id, order_id) WHERE status = 'pending'</code>. Plan modes were forced to expose the distinction. No automatic switch to a generic plan or general speed ratio is claimed.</p></figure>
<script>
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll('[data-r34-prepared]')){const select=root.querySelector('select');const draw=()=>{const m=select.value,g=m==='generic';root.querySelector('[data-predicate]').textContent=g?'shop_id = $1 AND status = $2':m==='literal'?"shop_id = $1 AND status = 'pending'":"shop_id = 20 AND status = 'pending'";root.querySelector('[data-proof]').textContent=g?'Unknown $2 might be paid. The pending-only index cannot cover every permitted answer.':"The answer lies within status = 'pending'.";root.querySelector('[data-route]').textContent=g?'Sequential scan → top-N sort → Limit 10':'Ordered index-only scan → Limit 10';root.querySelector('[data-result]').textContent=g?'2,048 local buffer accesses at Limit; 1,000 scan rows sorted; 10 returned.':'3 local buffer accesses at Limit; 10 rows returned.'};select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw()}
</script>
